@mischnic Where should I write the test case? 
`packages\core\package-manager\test\NodePackageManager.test.js` OR `packages\core\core\test\ParcelConfig.test.js`

In `ParcelConfig.test.js` file, a test case - `should error with a codeframe if a plugin is not resolved` is already written and it passes if `err.code === MODULE_NOT_FOUND && !options.shouldAutoInstall`. - which is what our fix is for. This means that if we add a hint as you have mentioned, it would show both the message - `Cannot find module foo, did you mean bar` AND `Auto install is disabled. please install this package manually and restart Parcel.`
